            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>Friday nights are a banger in Asheville, North Carolina (milepost 382), when drummers, tambourinists, djembefolas, and percussionists of all kinds gather in the heart of downtown for a tradition that’s now a quarter-century old — <a href="https://www.exploreasheville.com/article/ashevilles-weekly-drum-circle-local-tradition">the weekly drum circle</a>. </p><p><br></p><p>Even if you don’t play, it’s the perfect place to dawn a flowing skirt or fringe vest, feel the vibes, and wave your hands in the air like you’re at Woodstock, circa 1969. </p><p><br></p><p>While in town, you might also check out local eats like <a href="https://www.goodhotfish.com">Good Hot Fish</a>, which riffs on traditional North Carolina fish camps, or <a href="https://www.potentialnewbf.com">Potential New Boyfriend</a>, a vinyl listening lounge famed for its small plates and desserts.</p></div>
